    browser_session_fetch_body_not_disturbed_and_timer_rollback_2026-08-21, 990, "2026-11-09 p3-browser sweep: left open - defect #1 is a four-way duplicated JS engine where only the gc_async_mut copy implements the WHATWG disturbed-body rule (single-sourcing needed, not a 3x port); defect #2 (timer rollback publication) is unroot-caused. JS-engine/browser-session lane."
    browser_session_fetch_body_not_disturbed_and_timer_rollback_2026-08-21, 1127, "2026-11-27 W6-1 fixed & verified: single-sourced WHATWG disturbed-body rule and header/media helpers into src/lib/common/js/engine/response_body.spl, exported NATIVE_RESPONSE_ARRAY_BUFFER = -86 in src/lib/common/js/engine/runtime.spl, wired gc_async_mut/nogc_async_mut/nogc_sync_mut JS engine copies through the shared helper, added deep .clone() across Environment/EnvironmentStack/CallFrame/ObjectStore/JsInterpreter/JsRuntime/BrowserRuntimeState so transactional eval_script/advance_time/_flush_runtime_side_effects_and_pump_history rollback does not alias mutated runtime state, moved _snapshot_current_history_for_departure and sibling history helpers into browser_session.spl, and restored rebase-truncated assertions in browser_session_async_spec.spl. Verified via wa3_shared_bin/simple.exe --mode=interpreter: browser_session_async_spec.spl 25/25 (0 failures, outcome=OK) and browser_session_dom_generation_runtime_spec.spl 1/1 (0 failures, outcome=OK). close_evidence reproducer=test/01_unit/lib/common/web/browser_session_async_spec.spl prevention=test/01_unit/lib/common/web/browser_session_dom_generation_runtime_spec.spl"
